# Docs Rendering Elements

This rule documents the rendering capabilities of the planton.ai docs site — what the Markdown renderer supports, Mermaid diagram syntax, and element formats. It does NOT cover visual strategy decisions (when to use which diagram type, Napkin.ai workflows, asciinema workflows, density targets); those live in `@15-planton-ai-docs-visual-strategy` loaded via `@update-planton-ai-docs`.

## Mermaid Diagrams

**Version**: Mermaid v11.10.1
**Renderer**: `src/components/common/MermaidDiagram.tsx` (client-side, dark theme)
**Detection**: `src/components/common/CodeBlock.tsx` auto-detects `language-mermaid` fenced blocks

### Basic Syntax

````markdown
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[User] --> B[Planton] --> C[Cloud]
```
````

### Animated Edges (v11 feature)

Animated dashed lines for showing data flow, sync patterns, and request routing:

````markdown
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  CLI["planton CLI"]
  Platform["Planton"]
  Runner["Runner"]
  Cloud["Cloud API"]

  CLI -- request --> Platform
  Platform tunnel@-- secure tunnel --> Runner
  Runner -- execute --> Cloud

  tunnel@{animate: true}
```
````

Edge naming: `tunnel@`, `sync@`, `deploy@` — descriptive, not `a@`, `b@`.
Maximum 2-3 animated edges per diagram.

### Supported Diagram Types

| Type | Syntax | Best For |
|------|--------|----------|
| Flowchart | `flowchart LR/TB` | Decision logic, workflow steps |
| Sequence diagram | `sequenceDiagram` | Multi-service request flows |
| State diagram | `stateDiagram-v2` | Lifecycle transitions |
| ER diagram | `erDiagram` | Data model relationships |

### Mermaid Rules

- Do NOT use inline `style` attributes — the dark theme handles styling
- Keep node count under 12 (wider diagrams break mobile)
- Use subgraphs for bounded contexts: `subgraph runner [Customer Infrastructure]`
- Label edges descriptively: `-- creates -->` not `-->`

## Screenshot Placeholders

Hidden HTML comments — invisible to users, scannable for future screenshot collection:

```html
<!-- SCREENSHOT: {context}
  Page: {web console path}
  Action: {what state the UI should be in}
  Focus: {what to highlight or crop to}
  Alt: {accessibility text for the future image}
-->
```

All four fields required. Place immediately before or after the referencing paragraph.

## Images

All images use the Cloudflare R2 CDN. See `@03-planton-ai-docs-media` for URL format and conventions.

```markdown
![Alt text](https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/docs/{section}/{page}/{filename}.png)
```

### Figures with Captions

```html
<figure>
  <img src="https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/docs/..." alt="Descriptive text" />
  <figcaption>Optional caption.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

## Callouts

```markdown
> **Note:** This feature requires organization-level permissions.

> **Tip:** Use `planton --help` to discover available subcommands.

> **Warning:** Rotating credentials will interrupt currently running jobs.
```

## Code Blocks

Supported language tags for syntax highlighting: `bash`, `yaml`, `json`, `ts`, `tsx`, `js`, `go`, `java`, `proto`, `hcl`, `dockerfile`, `sql`, `diff`, `text`, `mermaid`

Placeholders use angle brackets: `<org-id>`, `<env-name>`.

## Collapsible Sections

```html
<details>
  <summary>Show detailed architecture</summary>

  [Detailed content here]

</details>
```

## Don'ts

- No MDX components (`<Tabs/>`, `<Card/>`, `<Callout/>`) — not supported by the current renderer
- No local image paths or GitHub URLs — use Cloudflare R2
- No secrets, tokens, or PII in code, screenshots, or logs
- No `style` attributes in Mermaid diagrams

## Where Visual Strategy Lives

The documentation visual strategy (diagram taxonomy, when to animate, Napkin.ai prompt workflows, asciinema recording workflows, visual density targets, asset review protocol) lives in the planton monorepo at `@15-planton-ai-docs-visual-strategy`, loaded via `@update-planton-ai-docs`.
